  "worked_solution": "To find the expression, let's apply each of the transformations in turn.\n\n1\\. Stretching the graph of $y=f(x)$ by a scale factor of $5$ parallel to the $y$-axis is equivalent to multiplying the function expression by $5.$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=5f(x).\n  $$\n\n2\\. Translating the graph of $y=5f(x)$ up by $2$ units is equivalent to adding $2$ to the function expression. Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=5f(x)+2.\n  $$\n\n3\\. Translating the graph of $y=5f(x)+2$ by $4$ units to the right is equivalent to replacing every instance of $x$ with $(x-4).$ Applying this transformation, we obtain \n\n  $$\n  y=5f(x-4)+2.\n  $$\n\nTherefore, the final function expression is $y=5f(x-4)+2.$",
